  "claim": "Arne Berge helped rescue the inmates of a concentration camp during operation White Buses.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Arne Berge. Sentence: Arne Berge (29 June 1908 – 13 August 1988) was a Norwegian priest.\nPage: Arne Berge. Sentence: He was seamen's priest in Hamburg during World War II, when he also worked among Scandinavian prisoners in Germany, and helped planning and carrying out the White Buses operation.\nPage: White Buses. Sentence: \"White Buses\" was an operation undertaken by the Swedish Red Cross and the Danish government in the spring of 1945 to rescue concentration camp inmates in areas under Nazi control and transport them to Sweden, a neutral country.",
